styles=getSampleStyleSheet(); styles.add(ParagraphStyle(name='TitleCenter',parent=styles['Title'],alignment=TA_CENTER,spaceAfter=14)); styles['BodyText'].fontSize=9; styles['BodyText'].leading=11.5; styles['BodyText'].spaceAfter=5
story=[]
def P(text,style='BodyText'): story.append(Paragraph(text,styles[style]))
def H(text): P(text,'Heading1')
def T(rows,widths=None):
 t=Table(rows,colWidths=widths,repeatRows=1,hAlign='LEFT');t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#dbeafe')),('GRID',(0,0),(-1,-1),.3,colors.grey),('FONTSIZE',(0,0),(-1,-1),8),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5)]));story.append(t);story.append(Spacer(1,10))
def Img(path,w=6.6*inch,h=2.7*inch):story.append(Image(str(output/path),width=w,height=h));story.append(Spacer(1,6))
P('PathSnap — Technical Report','TitleCenter');P('Team review draft · 18 November 2026','Heading3');P('<b>Status:</b> This draft records executed experiments and known gaps. The team must verify the official scoring rule and all required submission assets before submission. No evaluator-test data was used for model selection.')
H('1. Problem and system');P('Noisy GPS observations are matched to directed road arcs. A candidate generator identifies nearby segments, a baseline or trained classifier scores candidates, and a Viterbi decoder uses movement and road connectivity to choose per-observation matches. FastAPI serves the results to a React/Leaflet map. Intermediate road paths are not expanded by the current decoder.')
H('2. Dataset and preprocessing');P('The supplied development data has 80 training and 10 student-test trips. Each trip contains track, nodes, arcs, and where supplied an ordered route. Candidate generation uses a local metric projection, a 50 m radius, and at most eight directed arcs per observation. It preserves coordinate order and timestamps, and records observations with no candidates.')
P('The route is an ordered sequence without observation timestamps. Monotone alignment estimates labels independently of inference candidates, allows stays and skips, and marks ambiguous, distant and disconnected cases. These are inferred proxy labels, not verified observation-level ground truth. Training folds keep entire trips together. Learned imputation is fitted only on the training fold.')
T([['Partition','GPS points','Confident proxy','Ambiguous','Unavailable'],['Training','208,417','69,372','61,133','77,912'],['Student test','19,160','9,118','8,529','1,513']],[85,75,105,90,90]);P('Training: 491 confident labels miss the candidate shortlist; student test: 16. Student-test trip 00000052 was inspected earlier, so student-test is development data rather than a fully untouched test. Candidate misses count as wrong in top-1; ambiguous and unavailable points are not included in that denominator.')
Img('trip_map.png',6.3*inch,3.5*inch);P('Figure: real training trip 00000005, raw GPS in blue and independently drawn midpoint-decoder matched segments in red. The interactive Folium preview is generated by src.routing.map_preview.')
story.append(PageBreak());H('3. Features and model comparisons');P('The distance-only baseline uses a normalized exponential distance score. Heading agreement is the cosine of the incoming GPS motion and directed arc orientation. Heading is missing for short movements under 5 m, nonpositive or over-10-second intervals, first observations and degenerate roads; the estimator uses its training-fitted imputer. Four additional candidate features were evaluated: distance margin, projected position, distance rank and segment length. A separate versioned export retained the original labels and trip folds. The four-feature configuration uses distance, heading, margin and position; the six-feature configuration adds rank and length.')
P('Five four-feature classifiers were trained. The table reports pooled classifier-only student-test agreement against confident inferred labels, with candidate misses counted as incorrect; candidate-level precision, recall, F1 and binary log loss condition on reference-candidate presence.')
rows=[['Model','Top-1','Precision','Recall','Macro F1','Log loss']]
for label,n in zip(labels,names):
 v=student['models'][n];rows.append([label,f"{100*v['top1_including_misses']:.2f}%",f"{v['candidate_positive_precision']:.3f}",f"{v['candidate_positive_recall']:.3f}",f"{v['candidate_macro_f1']:.3f}",f"{v['candidate_binary_log_loss']:.3f}"])
T(rows,[110,70,70,65,75,70]);Img('student_heading.png',6.3*inch,2.7*inch);Img('cv_heading.png',6.3*inch,2.7*inch);Img('f1_comparison.png',6.3*inch,2.7*inch)
P('The following selected-model ablation uses the same frozen training folds and later development-trip comparisons. Student-test has already been inspected; it is not an untouched final test.')
T([['Features','Training CV proxy','Student projected proxy'],['Distance + heading','79.98%','85.44%'],['Four features','80.84%','86.05%'],['Six features','80.85%','85.42%']],[150,140,150])
P('Logistic regression offers an interpretable linear comparison but emitted local numerical-library warnings; reproduce in a clean environment. Gaussian naive Bayes is fast but assumes conditional feature independence. The depth-limited decision tree captures nonlinear boundaries but may overfit. Random forest adds ensemble stability at higher runtime. Histogram gradient boosting captures nonlinear interactions efficiently and achieved 84.42% classifier-only student-test proxy agreement, while Gaussian naive Bayes achieved 84.88% but had worse conditional candidate log loss. The student-test table uses separately refitted models; the paired routing table below uses the earlier sorted-data model. Training order changes their predictions. The observations support only a provisional choice; actual generalization and calibration require stronger reference labels.')
story.append(PageBreak());H('4. Bayesian tuning');P('A six-trial Gaussian-process expected-improvement search tuned the four-feature histogram model over max_leaf_nodes 7–63, selecting 15 versus the default 31 using training-trip candidate binary log loss. The same training folds produced untuned/tuned macro F1 of 0.8739/0.8754 and binary log loss of 0.20352/0.20346; the tuned CV estimate is selection-biased. On the same student-test proxy labels, classifier top-1 was 84.42%/84.68%, candidate macro F1 was 0.8994/0.8984 and binary log loss was 0.16927/0.16988. No artificial epoch curves are shown. The demo uses the untuned four-feature model, already tested end to end.')
H('5. Routing and evaluation');P('The hidden states are candidate directed arcs. Emissions are classifier or distance scores normalized per observation; transitions penalize discrepancy between road travel distance and GPS displacement, subject to directed reachability and a speed limit. The Viterbi recurrence chooses the best prior state plus transition and current emission in log space. Missing candidates, nonpositive timestamps, large gaps and unreachable transitions end a block and emit diagnostics. The experimental projected policy estimates arc entry and exit positions, with a documented jitter rule and midpoint fallback.')
T([['Scorer','Decoder','Proxy agreement','Resets'],['Distance','Classifier only','54.53%','N/A'],['Distance','Midpoint','50.27%','753'],['Distance','Projected','85.51%','126'],['Heading model','Classifier only','83.36%','N/A'],['Heading model','Midpoint','75.31%','753'],['Heading model','Projected','85.44%','126']],[110,110,130,75]);P('The six runs share candidates and the 9,118-confident-label denominator. Projected routing improves proxy agreement in this comparison but has 126 reset events and can regress on individual segments. The projected audit uses the same distance policy and is not independent proof of correctness. Two independently reported classifier/midpoint counts differ; local reruns reproduced the counts shown here. The cause is unresolved. This report does not establish a 95% official accuracy.')
H('6. API and deployment');P('Laptop 1 hosts FastAPI and local data/artifact; Laptop 2 loads trips and submits a selection over the network. The UI shows mode, decoder, GPS, unmatched observations and reset markers. Local verification covered a live frontend/backend prediction on trip 00000005 and API error handling. A second laptop loaded the UI and sent trip 00000005 to the trained-model backend; the user confirmed that the map and prediction worked, and the backend log recorded the separate client. See README for exact commands. The provisional demo choice is the four-feature histogram classifier with projected routing, subject to team and final evaluation review.')
H('7. Remaining verification');P('Obtain the official reference/scoring method; validate on the reserved evaluator partition only at final evaluation; repeat the two-laptop demonstration in the final evaluation environment; independently reproduce numerical warnings; and inspect the remaining development-tool dependency advisory. Generated trained artifacts are local and have not been published. The team must verify and explain this report and make its final submission decisions.')
SimpleDocTemplate(str(output/'PathSnap_technical_report_DRAFT.pdf'),pagesize=(612,792),rightMargin=54,leftMargin=54,topMargin=50,bottomMargin=50,title='PathSnap technical report draft').build(story)
